The legal texts are Acts of the Kingdom of Tonga as published by the Attorney General's Office
(Tongan Legislation, https://www.ago.gov.to), in the 1988, 2016 and 2020 Revised Editions.

The site states: "Legislation can be downloaded and printed for private use. Any commercial entity is required to
obtain permission to reuse the data." Lexifina relies instead on the Copyright Act 2002 of Tonga (now Cap. 17.05,
2020 Revised Edition), section 5, "Subject matter not protected":

  "Notwithstanding the provisions of section 3 and 4, no protection under this Act shall extend to -
   ... (b) any official text of a legislative, administrative or legal nature, or any official translation thereof."

(Text as published by WIPO Lex, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/edocs/lexdocs/laws/en/to/to003en.pdf.) The Acts in
this repository are official texts of a legislative nature and are therefore not protected by copyright in Tonga.

Changes made by Lexifina: each edition was converted from the PDF text layer to one Markdown file per provision;
headers, footers, endnote markers and editorial notes were left out, and the editions were arranged as git commits
dated by the Attorney General's legislation history table. The wording of the law was not changed. The Attorney
General's Office does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
